    {
      "id": "credimi-collaborative-automation-for-eudi-interoperability-and-conformance-pYLePZ",
      "sector": "public_sector",
      "title": "Credimi: Collaborative Automation for EUDI Interoperability and Conformance",
      "summary": "Credimi is a shared automation and evidence platform for EUDI Wallet interoperability and conformance testing. It lets real wallets, issuers and verifiers from different countries and ecosystems be exercised in repeatable combinations, replacing bilateral demonstrations and manual testing with reusable workflows.\n\nThe platform automates both API interactions and end-user wallet journeys across physical or virtual devices. It captures structured results, protocol metadata, screenshots, video and device logs, then maps that evidence to a maintained source of truth covering EUDI ARF, OpenID, ETSI and regulatory requirements.\n\nCredimi also translates Functional Conformance Assessment Framework (FCAF) test specifications into repeatable automated test journeys and reviewable evidence. Our implementation of the FCAF tests, will be presented at GDC 2026 on Day 2 at 14:00 in Room F.\n\nThe collaboration value is cumulative: each implementation added to the environment creates new interoperability combinations for the wider community. Developers, pilots, Member States and assessors can reproduce failures, compare behaviour, share findings and rerun the same tests after fixes.",
      "organizationName": "Forkbomb",
      "productionDeployment": "yes",
      "status": "published",
